      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_chimpanzee_comparison",
      "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Comparing Black People to Primates",
      "description": "This stereotype, rooted in racist history, involves portraying Black individuals as inferior, animalistic, or unintelligent by likening them to primates. It is a deeply harmful and offensive trope used to demean and dehumanize Black people. In this meme, the chimpanzee image is used to mock Michelle Obama, a Black woman, implying she is 'animal-like' or unintelligent, which is a direct invocation of this racist stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f63d7f13"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_da87f05a",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "michelle_obama",
      "label": "Michelle Obama",
      "description": "Michelle Obama is the former First Lady of the United States, wife of former President Barack Obama. She is a prominent public figure, advocate, and former U.S. government official. Her public image is associated with intelligence, grace, and leadership. The meme attempts to undermine her by associating her with a primate, which is a racist attack on her identity and intellect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
